#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186097833 :tutorial/content "A **unit vector** is a vector whose magnitude is equal to $1.$ \n\nGiven any vector $\\mathbf a$, we can create a unit vector $\\mathbf u$ by dividing $\\mathbf a$ by its magnitude $|\\, \\mathbf{a} \\,|,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{u} = \\dfrac{ \\mathbf{a} }{ |\\,\\mathbf{a}\\,| }\n$$\n\nFor example, if $|\\,\\mathbf{a}\\,|=2,$ then the unit vector is\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{u} = \\dfrac{\\mathbf{a}}{2} = \\dfrac{1}{2} \\mathbf{a}.\n$$\n\n![](images/c7/c78d5b75c1d5928e7b269a4a67229487b3d3324e9815b11c5fd1f47f63437d82.png)" :tutorial/id #uuid "a90fd4b3-d41f-589f-9067-39d57e3e8712" :tutorial/math-academy-id 2906 :tutorial/title "Introduction"}]}
